 "_about": "Philippine nationwide holidays as DECLARED by the government, per year: the regular holidays, special (non-working) days and additional special (non-working) days of each year's proclamation, with the later proclamations that moved, added or removed days (Eid'l Fitr, Eid'l Adha, elections, bridge days) already applied; a 'note' says where a day was moved from. Special WORKING days are working days and are not listed: the EDSA anniversary on Feb 25 (2022, 2025-2027), and November 2, December 24 and December 31 of 2021 (Proclamation No. 1107) and of 2022 (Proclamation No. 1236). Local holidays of single cities or provinces and the regional Muslim holidays under PD 1083 (Amun Jadid, Maulidin Nabi, Lailatul Isra Wal Mi'raj) are not listed. Eid'l Fitr and Eid'l Adha of a year whose proclamation has not been issued are listed as 'pending' (2027), not given a guessed date. All Souls' Day (Nov 2) is listed in 2020, 2023, 2024, 2026 and 2027, where it was declared, and in 2025 at the product owner's request (Proclamation No. 727 names only October 31 and November 1); in 2021 and 2022 it was a special working day. Sources: Official Gazette of the Philippines (officialgazette.gov.ph/nationwide-holidays/{year}), Malacanang / PCO and PNA releases, the proclamation texts (Supreme Court E-Library, Lawphil). To correct or extend a year, edit its entry here: [date, name, type, optional note] with type regular | special | islamic.",
